  "title": "Vowel Stretch",
  "statement": "A singer wants the k-letter stretch of a lyric line that has the most vowels to hold a long note. Return the largest number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u) in any k consecutive letters of line.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "line = \"rhythmicaudio\", k = 4",
      "output": "3"
    },
    {
      "input": "line = \"xyz\", k = 2",
      "output": "0"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= k <= line.length <= 100000",
    "line has lowercase letters only"
  ],
  "answerKey": {
    "pattern": "Fixed-size sliding window with a count",
    "keyPoints": [
      "Count vowels in the first k letters",
      "Slide: add 1 if the entering letter is a vowel, subtract 1 if the leaving letter is",
      "Keep the largest count"
    ],
    "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "edgeCases": [
      "No vowels",
      "Only vowels",
      "k equals the length"
    ],
    "acceptableSlowerApproaches": [
      "Count each window from scratch: O(n · k)"
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "The stretch always has k letters. How does the vowel count change when it moves by one letter?",
    "Only the entering and the leaving letter matter.",
    "Keep a count; add 1 for a vowel entering, subtract 1 for a vowel leaving, and track the maximum."
  ],
